<title>FRANCE: French in favour of Fr. Telecom sale-poll.</title>
<headline>French in favour of Fr. Telecom sale-poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A majority of French people would approve with a sale of a minority stake in France Telecom, whose privatisation is currently suspended by the new Socialist-led government, according to an opinion poll by the CSA institute.</p>
<p>According a poll of 1,000 people for the Nouvel Observateur weekly, a majority of French people said the new government should continue with the previous centre-right government's plans to partially privatise France Telecom to make it more dynamic in the face of competition.</p>
<p>Fifty-one percent of those polled said the new government should go ahead, while 35 percent said it should abandon the project and preserve a public service in the telecommunications sector.</p>
<p>According to the poll the French would prefer partial privatisations of bank Credit Lyonnais, Thomson and Air France rather than full privatisations.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
